import "res://Visual Novel Romance/gd/Intro.gd" as snippets

~ start
do MusicManager.play_music_for("res://Visual Novel Romance/music/alarm-clock.mp3", 2.0)
do MusicManager.play_music("res://Visual Novel Romance/music/music1.ogg")
{{GameData.player_name}}: Ugh... here we go again. Another day at university [ID:461A36_1DB06F]
{{GameData.player_name}}: Felix, you came to sleep on top of me again [ID:461A36_90182D]
{{GameData.player_name}}: Well, how can I start the day? [ID:461A36_B45121]

- Have breakfast [ID:461A36_6F23FA]
    => breakfast

- Go back to sleep [ID:461A36_E4CF67]
    => sleep_more

~ breakfast

do SaveManager.set_checkpoint("breakfast")
do GameData.morning_route = "breakfast"
do SceneController.fade_to_black()

You head to the kitchen to prepare your breakfast [ID:461A36_FA6005]

do SceneController.play_video("res://Visual Novel Romance/files/Breakfast_high.ogv")

{{GameData.player_name}}: Nothing could be better than this [ID:461A36_6192A7]

Felix sits on the table beside you, staring at your breakfast as if he hasn't eaten in days [ID:461A36_113DE2]

Despite his dramatic expression, he finished his own meal only a few minutes ago [ID:461A36_009442]

After breakfast, you finish getting ready and head to the university [ID:461A36_CD75C2]

do SceneController.stop_video()
do SceneController.change_background("res://Visual Novel Romance/files/img2.png")

When you arrive, you meet your friend from the History department. [ID:461A36_7A8F9B]

do SceneController.show_character("Sprite1")

Gio: Hey, {{GameData.player_name}}. Do you remember my last study about local folklore? I found more information about the stories we used to hear when we were children [ID:461A36_E57E16]

You begin to remember the tales about dreams, where an Oneiric being protects the dreams of children and the world itself, keeping balance between them [ID:461A36_FC21AE]

The legend says that when people stop dreaming, the Oneirics lose their strength, leaving humanity vulnerable to the attacks of their greatest nightmares [ID:461A36_7F7656]

Gio: Well, according to the book I'm reading, these stories are ancient and connected to rituals and ancestral temples [ID:461A36_797C3E]

Gio: This book suggests that, if those practices truly worked, people could reach a state where they were able to control their dreams. Dreams could even become a way to understand the present or glimpse the future [ID:461A36_C773C5]

Gio: I'm going to use this book for my research project. What did you think about it? [ID:461A36_CBA733]

- Ask more about it [ID:461A36_64E24E]
  => about

- Remember the childhood tales [ID:461A36_A83E08]
  => tales

~ about
do SaveManager.set_checkpoint("about")

{{GameData.player_name}}: That's incredible. Is this book from the university? I'd love to hear more about your research [ID:461A36_EB163B]

Gio: Actually, I borrowed it from a small chapel not far from here. There are plenty of academic books on the subject, but I wanted firsthand accounts from people who actually lived through those experiences [ID:461A36_81BAB0]

Gio: That's what makes this one so fascinating. It was written by a monk who documented his entire journey, from his first encounters with those practices to the day he became a monk himself [ID:461A36_131995]

The two of you continue talking until it's time for class [ID:461A36_0CBE6D]

Once inside the classroom, you struggle to stay awake. After managing to copy a few notes, the lecture finally comes to an end [ID:461A36_49ED75]

As everyone begins to leave, Gio catches up with you [ID:461A36_D10BD0]

Gio: Heading home? Want to walk together? [ID:461A36_EF8DFE]

You nod, and the two of you leave the university side by side [ID:461A36_17EB14]

=> work

~ tales
do SaveManager.set_checkpoint("tales")

{{GameData.player_name}}: So... the stories our parents used to tell us actually came from this folklore? [ID:461A36_77128B]

{{GameData.player_name}}: There were so many of them, but I can barely remember any now [ID:461A36_B7226D]

Gio: That's right. Over time, most people simply forgot them. Even so, many older generations still hold on to those legends [ID:461A36_8BB3BC]

Gio: We even have festivals and traditions that keep the stories alive, though they're nothing like they used to be [ID:461A36_E24D94]

{{GameData.player_name}}: I loved listening to those stories when I was a kid. But eventually everyone stopped talking about them [ID:461A36_992488]

{{GameData.player_name}}: I remember attending ceremonies where people encouraged us to treasure our dreams and never give up on them [ID:461A36_1385B1]

Gio: That's one of the core beliefs behind these traditions [ID:461A36_DBCB22]

Gio: Dreams are said to reveal who we truly are... or, sometimes, the parts of ourselves we're trying to hide [ID:461A36_A9FF05]

Gio: To stop dreaming, or to stop pursuing your goals, is like turning your back on your own identity [ID:461A36_847A38]

{{GameData.player_name}}: That's... actually a really interesting way of looking at it [ID:461A36_1698F6]

{{GameData.player_name}}: I'd better get going. My class has probably already started [ID:461A36_E19B7F]

Gio: See you around. [ID:461A36_7678AC]
do SceneController.hide_character("Sprite1")

You make your way to class, though staying awake proves to be a challenge [ID:461A36_C1A776]

After scribbling down a few notes, the lecture finally ends [ID:461A36_419A90]

As you're leaving campus, Gio catches up with you [ID:461A36_4D27BF]
do SceneController.show_character("Sprite1")

Gio: Ready to head home? [ID:461A36_6D0714]

You agree, and the two of you walk away from the university together [ID:461A36_EE8152]

do SceneController.hide_character("Sprite1")

