	Gio: Hey, {{GameData.player_name}}. How are you? [ID:461A36_B03394]
	Gio: Do you remember my last study about local folklore? I found more information about the stories we used to hear when we were children [ID:461A36_2D3E40]
	You begin to remember the tales about dreams, where an Oneiric being protects the dreams of children and the world itself, keeping balance between them [ID:461A36_D729F7]
	The legend says that when people stop dreaming, the Oneirics lose their strength, leaving humanity vulnerable to the attacks of their greatest nightmares [ID:461A36_15EE3F]
	Gio: Well, according to the book I'm reading, these stories are ancient and connected to rituals and ancestral temples [ID:461A36_2DA8B9]
	Gio: This book suggests that, if those practices truly worked, people could reach a state where they were able to control their dreams. Dreams could even become a way to understand the present or glimpse the future [ID:461A36_50A223]
	Gio: I'm going to use this book for my research project. [ID:461A36_D7699D]
	
	- talk about your cat [ID:461A36_76AD4D]
